1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,737
Every Seeker came with an address,
and nobody ever writes to it.

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,997
So we built Penny Post, a
letterbox for your wallet.

3
00:00:09,247 --> 00:00:12,008
Every morning it brings one
question for everyone,

4
00:00:12,008 --> 00:00:14,216
and everyone who answers shares the pot.

5
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:19,600
It brings postcards too. A stranger
pays your price to reach you,

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,194
and you keep ninety percent.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,686
If you never open it, their
money goes back to them.

8
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:29,394
A paid message is only a gate on a chat.

9
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,297
This is the post, and it
comes once a day.

10
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:40,790
Here is the real app, live
on Solana devnet.

11
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:45,488
You don't even need a wallet to try
it. Choose the practice wallet,

12
00:00:45,488 --> 00:00:49,275
tap Set me up, and that one tap
gives you a letterbox.

13
00:00:49,275 --> 00:00:53,694
A few seconds later the morning post
arrives: today's question,

14
00:00:53,694 --> 00:00:55,026
and a welcome card.

15
00:00:57,871 --> 00:00:59,437
If you bring your own wallet,

16
00:00:59,437 --> 00:01:02,190
every signature goes through
Mobile Wallet Adapter.

17
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:08,317
Let me open today's question.
Somebody asked every Seeker,

18
00:01:08,317 --> 00:01:13,582
tea or coffee first thing, and put up
300 SKR for whoever answers.

19
00:01:13,582 --> 00:01:15,896
I pick tea, and approve once.

20
00:01:15,896 --> 00:01:20,044
The program checks my Seeker
Genesis Token on-chain,

21
00:01:20,044 --> 00:01:23,953
so one phone gets exactly one
answer. And I'm in.

22
00:01:23,953 --> 00:01:26,027
My share so far is 45 SKR.

23
00:01:28,994 --> 00:01:34,298
Now it is the next morning. Yesterday's
question has closed, tea won,

24
00:01:34,298 --> 00:01:39,218
and my share is waiting for me. There
is a new question as well.

25
00:01:39,218 --> 00:01:44,599
With a single signature, I collect
yesterday's SKR and answer today's.

26
00:01:44,599 --> 00:01:49,441
That is the whole habit: one tap
each morning, and it pays you.

27
00:01:49,441 --> 00:01:53,746
For this scene, we moved the test
clock forward one day.

28
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:59,350
The rest of the post comes
from people. Here,

29
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:03,170
a stranger has paid my price, 10
SKR, to send me a card.

30
00:02:03,170 --> 00:02:08,014
Their money sits in escrow. I can see
who it is from, and nothing more,

31
00:02:08,014 --> 00:02:12,653
until I sign for it. When I do, the
card slides out of its envelope,

32
00:02:12,653 --> 00:02:16,883
turns over, and 9 SKR is mine. If I
had ignored it for a week,

33
00:02:16,883 --> 00:02:19,407
they would have got their money back.

34
00:02:23,795 --> 00:02:27,816
I can write back. I write the message
with my finger, choose a stamp,

35
00:02:27,816 --> 00:02:31,312
and the app tells me what it costs,
and when it will arrive,

36
00:02:31,312 --> 00:02:33,818
before I sign anything.
The card is sealed,

37
00:02:33,818 --> 00:02:35,683
so only their phone can read it.

38
00:02:42,004 --> 00:02:44,096
On my profile, I set my own price.

39
00:02:44,096 --> 00:02:47,604
And any builder can ask every
Seeker tomorrow's question,

40
00:02:47,604 --> 00:02:49,388
simply by putting up the pot.

41
00:02:52,244 --> 00:02:56,565
That is Penny Post. It is live
on Solana devnet today,

42
00:02:56,565 --> 00:02:59,045
with an app anyone can install,

43
00:02:59,045 --> 00:03:03,446
tested against real SKR and real
Seeker Genesis Tokens.

44
00:03:03,446 --> 00:03:05,526
The post comes once a day.
